imbridge transport: the port comes from IMBRIDGE_PORT (default 45700 + uid - 501, so it never collides with
BlueBubbles Server); with IMBRIDGE_TOKEN set, requests must carry that token or get {"error": "unauthorized"};
requests are read one newline-terminated line at a time instead of one socket read each (which dropped or split
requests); the helper redials every second instead of every 5; logs go to the "imbridge" subsystem.

